---
title: Korean Cheesy Corn
description: A creamy, gooey Korean-style side dish of sweet corn baked with mayonnaise and mozzarella until bubbly and golden.
course: side
cuisine: Korean
servings: 4
time required: 17 minutes
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 12 minutes
source: https://www.spoonforkbacon.com/korean-cheesy-corn/
image: https://www.spoonforkbacon.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/korean-cheese-corn.jpg
tags: [korean, corn, cheese, side]
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 400°F.

In a #mixing bowl{}, combine @sweet corn kernels{2%ears}(kernels removed from cob), @mayonnaise{1/2%cup}, @shredded mozzarella{4%oz}, @sugar{1.5%tsp}, @green onions{2}(thinly sliced), @salt{} and @pepper{}, and stir together.

Pour the mixture into a lightly greased #baking dish{}.

Bake for ~{10%minutes}, or until the mixture melts and bubbles.

Transfer the dish to the broiler and broil for ~{2%minutes}, or until the top browns.

Serve immediately.
